00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.340
I realized that it's more than that pala.

53
00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:40.340
It actually helped me understand myself better
in different ways.

54
00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:52.340
First, I can't connect this to culture and
identity because Santacruzan is part of our
Filipino tradition and being part of it made
me appreciate our culture more.

55
00:04:52.340 --> 00:05:00.340
Napara bang it reminded me na our identity is
also shaped by the traditions and community we
grew up with.

56
00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:05.340
It also connects to my social self and social
influences.

57
00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:12.340
During the preparation of the event, I was
surrounded by people who helped and supported
me like my family,

58
00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.340
and the new friends ko, and the organizers of
the event.

59
00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:22.340
And honestly, malaking bagay yung support nila
because it made me feel more confident and
comfortable.

60
00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:28.340
Dun ko na-realize na the people around us can
really affect how we feel about ourselves.

61
00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:34.340
Another concept that I can relate to this is
self-esteem.

62
00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:40.340
At first, kinakabahan nga talaga ako kasi
especially knowing na marami people ngayong
manolood.

63
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.340
But while the event was happening, I slowly
felt more confident.

64
00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:51.340
Parang I proved to myself na kaya ko pala even
if I felt shy or nervous at first.

65
00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:59.340
This experience also reflects my physical self
because a big part of the preparation was
fixing my appearance of course

66
00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:05.340
like my gown, hair, makeup, and over-
presentation na patpresentable ka para

67
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:11.340
kung mga kamaganda sa procession, but for me,
it wasn't just about looking good.

68
00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:17.340
It was also about feeling good, being
confident, and presenting myself properly for
the event.

69
00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.340
My emotional self was also very present during
this experience.

70
00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:28.340
I felt excited, nervous, happy, and proud all
at the same time.

71
00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.340
Mixed emotions talaga siya.

72
00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:35.340
But I think that's what made the experience
more memorable for me.

73
00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:42.340
I can also connect this to my cognitive self
because I have to prepare, make decisions,
follow instructions,

74
00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.340
and think how I would handle myself during the
event.

75
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:51.340
And especially nakaroon ako ng problem sa
gown.

76
00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:57.340
And after everything, I also reflected on what
this experience taught me.

77
00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:05.340
And lastly, I can relate these two Maslow’s
hierarchy of needs, especially belongingness
and esteem needs.

78
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.340
Belongingness because I felt like I was part
of our community and tradition.

79
00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:20.340
And esteem needs because after the event, I
felt proud of myself for participating and for
stepping out of my comfort zone, especially
mahiyain nga talaga ako.

80
00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:27.340
So overall, the Santacruzan experience was not
just about wearing a gown or joining a
procession.

81
00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:37.340
It became a meaningful experience that taught
me how confidence, culture, community,
emotions, and personal growth.

